  "id": "behavioral-dynamics",
  "term": "behavioral dynamics",
  "definition": "Behavioral dynamics refers to changes in how organisms act and adapt within a system, especially strategies such as cooperation, non-cooperation, and infection-avoidance behaviors that can alter disease spread and population stability. In this context, it describes how patterns of behavior within and between groups shape ecological and epidemic outcomes.",
